    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nThe \"tag\" text object naively selects until it finds a matching closing tag, disregarding possible nesting. In this, it seems to be a regression over the native implementation of the tag text object, which works as expected (to the extent I tested it).\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.9.5\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUsing this `min-init.lua`:\r\n\r\n```\r\nlocal lazypath = \"/tmp/lazy/lazy.nvim\"\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazypath) then\r\n  vim.fn.system({ \"git\", \"clone\", \"--filter=blob:none\", \"https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git\", \"--branch=stable\", lazypath,\r\n  })\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.rtp:prepend(lazypath)\r\n\r\nrequire(\"lazy\").setup({\r\n  {\r\n    \"echasnovski/mini.ai\",\r\n    config = function(_, opts)\r\n      require(\"mini.ai\").setup(opts)\r\n    end,\r\n  },\r\n}, { root = \"/tmp/lazy\" })\r\n```\r\n\r\nand this `test.html` sample file:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<div>\r\n  <label>\r\n    <div>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </label>\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nrun NeoVim like this:\r\n\r\n```\r\nnvim --clean -u min-init.lua test.html\r\n```\r\n\r\nSitting at the start of the file, press `vat`. An analogous problem can also be observed with `vit`.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nI expect `vat` to select the whole file (around the outermost `<div>`). In fact, this is exactly the result NeoVim does by default. Running clean NeoVim:\r\n\r\n```\r\nnvim --clean -u none test.html\r\n```\r\n\r\n`vat` selects the following — correct — region:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<div>\r\n  <label>\r\n    <div>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </label>\r\n</div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nSimilarly, the expected selection for `vit` (also observed with clean NeoVim) is\r\n\r\n```\r\n  <label>\r\n    <div>\r\n    </div>\r\n  </label>\r\n```\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe selection incorrectly ends after the _inner_ div is closed, resulting in a selection:\r\n\r\n```\r\n<div>\r\n  <label>\r\n    <div>\r\n    </div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nIn the same way, the `vit` selection ends up as:\r\n\r\n```\r\n  <label>\r\n    <div>\r\n```",
