        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "'mini.ai' uses Lua patterns to search for the target region. This will inevitably result into false positives. It is a [known issue which won't be resolved'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/70d8a16399ca6df759d20bea302d6dfd710a1df8/doc/mini-ai.txt#L44-L45).\r\n\r\nTags is a main source of such false positives. In particular, I couldn't find a way to make it work with nested similar tags, like `<div>`s in your example. My suggestion would be to use tree-sitter grammar to properly parse structure and textobjects to have relevant queries. See [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/110#issuecomment-1212277863) for more information.\r\n\r\nClosing as duplicate of #156, #304, and #420.",
